> Does anyone under stand this code better than me?
>       register int area = (sroom->hx - sroom->lx) * (sroom->hy - sroom->ly);
>       return( area > 20 );

     This formula has a pair of off-by-1 bugs in it, unless the dimensions
are recorded with one of each low or high coordinate inside the room and
the other on the surrounding wall.  Since they're not recorded that way,
the calcuation above will yield 12 instead of 21 for your room, then
compare "wrong" versus 20.

     The room creation percentages you posted are also the victim of a
(much more subtle) off-by-1 bug, so that there's only a 2% chance that
any particular shop will be a spellbook store, not 3%.  General stores
benefit from the mis-assigned 1%.

